Title: The Short Film
Author: Demo Script
Draft date: January 2026

===

INT. APARTMENT - DAY

SARAH, late 20s, sits at her laptop typing furiously.

SARAH
(to herself)
Come on, come on...

Her phone buzzes. She ignores it.

EXT. COFFEE SHOP - DAY

JAMES, early 30s, waits outside with two coffees. He checks his watch.

JAMES
(into phone)
Sarah, where are you?

INT. APARTMENT - DAY - CONTINUOUS

SARAH
Sorry! I'm running late. The deadline--

JAMES (V.O.)
The deadline was yesterday.

SARAH
I know, I know. Give me ten minutes.

She hangs up and saves her document.

EXT. COFFEE SHOP - DAY

JAMES sits at an outdoor table. SARAH arrives, out of breath.

SARAH
I'm sorry. Traffic was--

JAMES
You don't have a car.

SARAH
(sitting)
Figurative traffic.

JAMES
(smiling)
You're impossible.

He hands her a coffee.

SARAH
You're the best.

They sit in comfortable silence.

JAMES
So... did you finish it?

SARAH
Almost. Just one more scene.

JAMES
The ending?

SARAH
Yeah. I can't figure out how to end it.

JAMES
What if you don't?

SARAH
Don't what?

JAMES
End it. Leave it open.

SARAH thinks about this.

SARAH
That's... actually brilliant.

JAMES
(shrugging)
I have my moments.

INT. SARAH'S APARTMENT - NIGHT

SARAH types the final words. She leans back, satisfied.

SARAH
(to herself)
Finally.

She closes her laptop and smiles.

FADE OUT.
